      "content": "6.1 IRDAI – Insurance Regulatory Authority of India"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "IRDAI functions as the statutory regulatory authority overseeing the Indian insurance industry.",
        "The sector is broadly divided into Life Insurance and General (Non-Life) Insurance.",
        "Key flagship government schemes aim to expand social security and cover agricultural, health, and accident risks.",
        "LIC (Life Insurance Corporation of India) remains the leading public sector life insurer in the country."
